                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='10400' id='28' type-v2='text' w='98858' x='571' y='88800'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Key findings</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>1. Heavier discounts go with slightly lower ratings: products discounted 80%+ average 3.97 stars, versus 4.17 for 0-20% (Spearman rho = -0.15).</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>2. Electronics, Home &amp; Kitchen and Computers &amp; Accessories make up about 97% of products, so conclusions about other categories are unreliable.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>3. Wearable Technology discounts hardest (about 70% on average), and Headphones, Earbuds &amp; Accessories has the lowest average rating among large sub-categories (3.92).</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' italic='true'>Findings are for the full dataset. Filters change the charts, not this text.</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#444444' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
              </zone>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#444444' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='8' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
          </zones>
        </devicelayout>
      </devicelayouts>
